  "rationale": "First baseline, re-recorded once before it was ever committed to correct three figures in this rationale that were read off a scratch probe rather than off this sweep. Values are unchanged; the probe used a different sweepId and therefore different run seeds. This sweep exists because the two cheap gates play no god verb at all: both run passive-control fixed, whose preference list is empty, so every action they submit is a noop and no god-agency change can move either of them by construction. That is not a tolerance problem and no statistic fixes it. Until now the only committed gate that put a strategy in front of the verbs was the 200-year ascension sweep, the most expensive instrument here and the one whose tolerances were widest. This one is the horizon gate's twenty-year cap with the ascension gate's eight-strategy round-robin pool -- the single declared difference from balance-gate-horizon-v1 is the pool, so a divergence between them is attributable to god agency and to nothing else. Measured on 2026-08-12 it separates the arms strongly at twenty years: referenceNodesKnown runs 5.00 (denial-warden) to 75.375 (permissive-breadth), a 15.1x spread; referenceLibraryDepth 3.25 to 37.75, 11.6x; and referenceNodesGainedFinalQuarter changes sign, -4.75 under denial-warden and -3.25 under narrow-depth against +17.00 under permissive-breadth -- universes losing distinct nodes faster than they find them. It costs 8.9 seconds on four workers against the ascension gate's 83.5.",
